====================================================================
JUDGEMENT ON THE FOUR KEYS (reasoning, not execution)
====================================================================
All four read as settled product Chinese rather than translation, and each is
consistent with an already-approved neighbour in this same locale:

  ui.chat.image_actions.actions = 图片操作
    Exact parallel of the existing ui.common.actions.file_actions_menu.file_actions
    = 文件操作 ("File actions"), and 图片 is the catalogue's established word for image
    (copy_image = 复制图片, expand_image = 展开图片). "Image actions" carries no plural
    in Chinese, which is correct rather than an omission. The sidecar asks for a
    short noun phrase for a tooltip and for the unnamed-image accessible-name
    fallback; a bare noun phrase satisfies both. No punctuation, no backticks.

  ui.chat.audio.position_label = {label}的播放位置
    {label} is byte-exact and stays first; only the surrounding word is translated,
    as the sidecar instructs. The construction is a plain attributive noun phrase, so
    it stays grammatical for any clip title — Latin filename, CJK title, title ending
    in punctuation, title containing “ ” quotes — with no case, gender or number
    agreement to break, and the zh-CN guide's no-space-between-Chinese-and-Latin rule
    is respected. Rendering "position" as 播放位置 rather than bare 位置 is the right
    call and not an addition of meaning: the sidecar's own first sentence is "Names
    playback position for this specific clip", and 播放位置 is the catalogue's existing
    term for exactly that concept (ui.chat.attachments.playback_position = 播放位置).
    Bare 位置 beside a file name would read as a spatial/screen position. It also
    stays distinguishable from the neighbouring verb-first play/pause names
    (播放{label}, 暂停{label}).

  ui.chat.composer_media.pasted_image = 粘贴的图片
    Mirror of the existing pasted_file = 粘贴的文件 and pasted_type = 粘贴的{mimeType}.
    Carries no file extension, no MIME identifier and no placeholder, as the sidecar
    requires, and it works as a filename. 10 cells against the sibling's 20-cell
    advisory budget; this key has no maxCells hint of its own.

  ui.common.actions.actions_for_name = {name}的操作
    Identical to two already-approved values for the identical English string —
    ui.chat.canonical.link_toolkit.actions_for = {name}的操作 and
    ui.projects.project_board.actions_for_displayname = {displayName}的操作 — and the
    same shape as ui.projects.project_updates.file_actions_for_name = {name}的文件操作.
    The 的-construction identifies the asset rather than commanding an action, which is
    what the sidecar asks for, and 操作 is the catalogue's term for "actions". Diverging
    from those three would have been the finding; matching them is not.
    Considered and dismissed: ui.browser.browser_tab_strip.actions_for wraps its
    {title} in “ ” (“{title}”的操作). That is a tab title, which can be a whole
    sentence; the two direct file/image precedents above are unquoted, so quoting here
    would introduce an inconsistency rather than remove one.

Nothing in the four values contradicts a §1 or §2 glossary row, because no product
name, no core §2 term and no kept-English token appears in them. The §3 rows that do
apply — placeholders byte-exact, Chinese punctuation conventions, no hand-written
digits, zh-CN "other"-only plurals — are all satisfied.

====================================================================
OBSERVATIONS THAT ARE NOT TRANSLATION FINDINGS
====================================================================
Raised so the manager can route them, and deliberately NOT counted against the
zh-CN translator, because both are locale-agnostic and both are equally true of the
English source:

  (a) Empty-label guard. image-actions-menu.tsx:364 guards the shared key with
      `label != null`, where supplement-file-actions.tsx:181 guards the same key with
      truthiness (`label ? ... :`). Callers pass label={alt} (markdown-image.tsx:90),
      label={document.title} and label={row.name}. An empty-string label — a markdown
      image with empty alt text is the plausible route — would satisfy `!= null` and
      call t("ui.common.actions.actions_for_name", { name: "" }), rendering "的操作"
      with a leading 的. The English degrades identically there ("Actions for "), so
      this is a source-side guard inconsistency, not a translation defect: the zh-CN
      value is right for every non-empty name. Not proven by execution — read from
      source only, and scripts/image-actions.test.mjs has no label/alt case.

  (b) Two keys for one English string. "Actions for {name}" now exists as both the
      legacy ui.chat.canonical.link_toolkit.actions_for and the new
      ui.common.actions.actions_for_name. check-duplicates passes because the keys
      differ, and both zh-CN values are identical today, so there is no current defect —
      recorded only as a future drift risk for whoever owns the keying change.

